# The .gitignore is authoritative on the versioned / local boundary, and every entry
# says WHY it is ignored — a readable .gitignore prevents case-by-case judgement, by
# a human as much as by an agent.
#
# Nothing is ignored here, and that is deliberate on both counts.
#
# Nothing private is ignored, because nothing private is here. What is private lives in
# a *copy* of this repository, downstream, on the machine that uses it — never in this
# tree, and never pushed back to it. A boundary drawn by structure holds against a
# mistyped command; one drawn by a rule in this file only holds while the rule does.
#
# ⚠ And `instance/` is NOT ignored, though it is the folder meant to hold private
# content. It ships empty on purpose. Ignoring it here would take effect inside every
# copy, where the folder is full — silently un-versioning the one corpus its owner
# most wants kept. An ignore rule written against this tree would then decide, at a
# distance, about a tree it has never seen.
